# Go tooling assumes LF, and the repository stores LF. Without this file and
# with core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout left part of the tree CRLF, which
# made `gofmt -l` name a different set of files on each run as git touched them
# — an [enforced] rule that could not be trusted. Pin the working tree to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entry points, which cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.exe binary
